// RT-CG-7 (fixed in 0.30.1): an integer saved in x17 (AArch64's integer cycle register) to break a cycle of an edge's moves was overwritten by the address of an f32 spill slot past 16 KB moved in the same plan (an f32 slot's offset is one ldr or str only below 16 KB), and the address was stored (tests/fuzz/genmoves.awk seed 210, pad=2100, as tests/fuzz/run.sh -F makes them; aarch64 -O1)
// FLAGS: -O1 --verify-regalloc
// EXPECT: 6
// EXPECT: 11
// EXPECT: 0
// EXPECT: 9
// EXPECT: 6.125
// EXPECT: 3.53125
// EXPECT: 14 10.5
// EXPECT: 4.5
// EXPECT: 7.5
// EXPECT: 12 5.5
// EXPECT: 15 5
// EXPECT: 3 7
// EXPECT: 1.9375
// EXPECT: 3.375
// EXPECT: 74 45.79365075100213
// EXPECT: 25893
// At -O1 the release branch printed other values on AArch64 (an address, which changes
// from run to run; x86-64 was right). The EXPECT lines are -O0's, which allocates no
// registers, and x86-64's. Now no spill access needs a scratch register
// (spill_access_type: an f32 slot from 16 KB on is read and written as its 8 bytes),
// ma_scratch refuses x17 while a plan's steps run, and --verify-regalloc follows the
// code of every plan (back/regalloc/movecode.vl).
